<header><p class="st-kicker">prince bishopric · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Imperial Abbey of Roggenburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1544 CE – 1802 CE (approx.) · capital Roggenburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Premonstratensian abbey in Swabia whose abbots ruled a small imperial territory between Ulm and Augsburg.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Roggenburg was founded in 1126 by the counts of Bibereck as a house of Premonstratensian canons. Raised to an abbey in 1444, it struggled for a century to free itself from outside advocates, and in 1544 its abbots won recognition of imperial immediacy.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The abbot governed a compact territory of villages in the hills between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iller">Iller</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunz">Günz</a> as a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-circle">Swabian Circle</a> and the Swabian bench of prelates. Farming and forestry provided income. Between 1752 and 1758 the canons built a large rococo church, which still stands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1802 the abbey was secularised and annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, and its library and treasures were dispersed. Premonstratensian canons returned in 1982, and Roggenburg is again a monastery.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="prince bishopric, 1544 CE – 1802 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">prince bishopric</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.43%;width:5.13%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1544 CE – 1802 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>prince bishopric</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Roggenburg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swabian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Germany</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Roggenburg Abbey</dd></dl></aside></div>
